Subject: [PATCH] clk: qcom: restore asynchronous runtime put for boot diagnosis

Local diagnostic rollback of the one-line difference from the working
7.2.6 clock-controller probe path. GPUCC uses desc->use_rpm; a synchronous
runtime suspend during registration is a candidate for the early boot failure.
This is not yet a confirmed root cause or an upstream-quality fix.

Keep the runtime-PM reference balancing, but defer the idle transition as
in the known-working kernel. No clock/DT/display-driver changes are included.

Reference: Linux 7.2.6 drivers/clk/qcom/common.c and the local 7.3.3 baseline.
Local change; no third-party patch or authorship is imported.

--- a/drivers/clk/qcom/common.c
+++ b/drivers/clk/qcom/common.c
@@ -428,7 +428,7 @@ int qcom_cc_really_probe(struct device *dev,
 
 put_rpm:
 	if (desc->use_rpm)
-		pm_runtime_put_sync(dev);
+		pm_runtime_put(dev);
 
 	return ret;
 }
